# SQLite-Backed Services CMS with Admin Panel

Replace hardcoded `serviceData.ts` with a SQLite database, a small Express API server, and a full admin panel at `/admin` so your client can manage services without touching code.

## Architecture Overview

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Browser                                                      │
│  ┌─────────────────┐     ┌─────────────────────────────┐    │
│  │  Existing App   │     │   /admin  (React route)      │    │
│  │  (Vite :5173)   │     │   Password-protected panel   │    │
│  └────────┬────────┘     └──────────────┬───────────────┘    │
│           │ fetch API                    │ fetch API          │
└───────────┼──────────────────────────────┼────────────────────┘
            ▼                              ▼
┌────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│  Express Server  :3001   (server/)                      │
│  ┌──────────────────────────────────────────────────┐  │
│  │  Routes                                           │  │
│  │  GET/POST/PUT/DELETE  /api/services               │  │
│  │  GET/POST/PUT/DELETE  /api/categories             │  │
│  │  POST                 /api/upload                 │  │
│  │  POST                 /api/auth/login             │  │
│  └───────────────────────┬──────────────────────────┘  │
│                          │                              │
│  ┌───────────────────┐   │   ┌──────────────────────┐  │
│  │  SQLite           │◄──┘   │  /public/uploads/    │  │
│  │  services.db      │       │  (images, etc.)      │  │
│  └───────────────────┘       └──────────────────────┘  │
└────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> The Express server runs on port **3001** alongside the Vite dev server on **5173**. In development you run both with `npm run dev`. In production, you would deploy the Express server separately (e.g., on a VPS or Railway.app) and point the frontend at its URL.

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Admin password** — We'll set a simple password stored in an env variable (`ADMIN_PASSWORD` in `.env`). This is protected by a session token in localStorage. If the client needs multi-user access later, Supabase Auth can be swapped in.

> [!WARNING]
> **Existing `serviceData.ts` data** — The entire hardcoded dataset (services + categories) will be **migrated into SQLite** as a seed script. The TypeScript file will be replaced with API calls. This is a one-way migration for services data.

---

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Backend — Express + SQLite server

#### [NEW] `server/index.js`
Entry point. Sets up Express, CORS, multer, and mounts all routes.

#### [NEW] `server/db.js`
Initializes better-sqlite3, creates tables, runs seed if empty.

**Database Schema:**
```sql
-- categories table
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS categories (
  id        TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  title     TEXT NOT NULL,
  description TEXT,
  requiresConsultation INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
  sortOrder INTEGER DEFAULT 0
);

-- services table
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS services (
  id                    TEXT PRIMARY KEY,
  name                  TEXT NOT NULL,
  price                 INTEGER NOT NULL,
  category              TEXT NOT NULL,
  categories            TEXT,          -- JSON array, e.g. '["consultation","hygiene"]'
  description           TEXT,
  detailedDescription   TEXT,
  duration              TEXT,
  heroImage             TEXT,
  backgroundPosition    TEXT,
  popular               INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
  isSpecialOffer        INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
  includesConsultation  INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
  requiresConsultation  INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
  benefits              TEXT,          -- JSON array
  process               TEXT,          -- JSON array
  suitableFor           TEXT,          -- JSON array
  faqs                  TEXT,          -- JSON array
  beforeAfterImages     TEXT,          -- JSON array
  serviceVideo          TEXT,
  galleryImages         TEXT,          -- JSON array
  sortOrder             INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
  createdAt             TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now')),
  updatedAt             TEXT DEFAULT (datetime('now'))
);
```

#### [NEW] `server/routes/services.js`
REST CRUD for services. Returns proper JSON, handles JSON column parsing.

#### [NEW] `server/routes/categories.js`
REST CRUD for categories.

#### [NEW] `server/routes/upload.js`
`multer` endpoint: `POST /api/upload` → saves to `public/uploads/` → returns the public URL.

#### [NEW] `server/routes/auth.js`
Simple password check. Returns a signed JWT stored in localStorage on the frontend.

#### [NEW] `server/seed.js`
One-time script that imports all data from `serviceData.ts`-equivalent JSON and inserts into SQLite.

#### [NEW] `server/middleware/auth.js`
JWT verification middleware that protects all write routes.

---

### 2. Frontend — API layer replacing static imports

#### [MODIFY] `src/types/serviceData.ts`
Keep interfaces (`PriceItem`, `ServiceCategory`) **but remove all hardcoded data constants** and replace helper functions with API-based versions. The file becomes types-only.

#### [NEW] `src/api/services.ts`
All API calls:
```ts
getServices(categoryId?: string): Promise<PriceItem[]>
getService(id: string): Promise<PriceItem>
getCategories(): Promise<ServiceCategory[]>
createService(data): Promise<PriceItem>
updateService(id, data): Promise<PriceItem>
deleteService(id): Promise<void>
createCategory(data): Promise<ServiceCategory>
updateCategory(id, data): Promise<ServiceCategory>
deleteCategory(id): Promise<void>
uploadFile(file: File): Promise<{ url: string }>
login(password: string): Promise<{ token: string }>
```

#### [MODIFY] `src/pages/PriceListPage.tsx`
Replace static imports with `useQuery` (TanStack Query, already installed) calls to the API.

#### [MODIFY] `src/pages/ServiceDetailPage.tsx`
Same — replace static data with an API fetch.

#### [MODIFY] `src/App.tsx`
Add `/admin` route (outside the main layout — no header/footer).

---

### 3. Admin Panel — `/admin` route

#### [NEW] `src/pages/admin/AdminLayout.tsx`
Wrapper with sidebar navigation and auth gate (redirects to login if no token).

#### [NEW] `src/pages/admin/AdminLoginPage.tsx`
Clean password login form. On success stores JWT in localStorage.

#### [NEW] `src/pages/admin/AdminDashboard.tsx`
Stats overview: total services, categories, recent additions.

#### [NEW] `src/pages/admin/ServicesListPage.tsx`
Table of all services with:
- Search & filter by category
- Edit / Delete buttons per row
- "Add service" button → opens form

#### [NEW] `src/pages/admin/ServiceFormPage.tsx`
Full form to create or edit a service. Fields:
- Name, category selector, price, duration
- Description (plain text)
- Detailed Description (textarea with markdown preview)
- Toggles: Popular, Special Offer, Requires Consultation, Includes Consultation
- Benefits (add/remove list)
- FAQs (add/remove pairs)
- Image upload for: Hero Image, Gallery Images, Before/After pairs
- Service video URL
- Sort order

#### [NEW] `src/pages/admin/CategoriesPage.tsx`
Manage category list: name, description, requiresConsultation toggle, order.

#### [NEW] `src/components/admin/ImageUploader.tsx`
Drag-and-drop image upload component — calls `/api/upload`, shows preview.

#### [NEW] `src/components/admin/MarkdownEditor.tsx`
Split-pane: left = textarea, right = rendered markdown preview (using existing `react-markdown`).

---

### 4. Dev tooling

#### [MODIFY] `package.json`
Add dependencies:
```json
// new dependencies
"better-sqlite3": "^9.x",
"express": "^4.x",
"cors": "^2.x",
"multer": "^1.x",
"jsonwebtoken": "^9.x",
"dotenv": "^16.x"
// new devDependencies
"@types/better-sqlite3": "^9.x",
"@types/multer": "^1.x",
"@types/jsonwebtoken": "^9.x",
"concurrently": "^8.x",
"nodemon": "^3.x"
```

Add scripts:
```json
"server":     "node server/index.js",
"server:dev": "nodemon server/index.js",
"dev":        "concurrently \"npm run server:dev\" \"vite\"",
"seed":       "node server/seed.js"
```

#### [NEW] `.env`
```
ADMIN_PASSWORD=changeme
JWT_SECRET=your-secret-key
PORT=3001
DB_PATH=./server/services.db
UPLOADS_DIR=./public/uploads
```

#### [MODIFY] `vite.config.ts`
Add proxy for API calls in dev:
```ts
server: {
  proxy: {
    '/api': 'http://localhost:3001'
  }
}
```

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated
- Run `npm run seed` → verify DB has all existing services
- `curl GET /api/services` → returns JSON array
- `curl GET /api/categories` → returns JSON array
- `curl POST /api/auth/login` with correct password → returns token
- Admin panel loads at `/admin` and redirects to login

### Manual
1. Open existing `/services` page → loads from API, looks identical
2. Open `/admin`, log in, see service list
3. Create a new service → appears on `/services` page
4. Edit a service → changes reflected immediately
5. Upload image → appears in `public/uploads/`, usable as heroImage
6. Delete a service → gone from list
7. Reorder categories → order reflects on frontend
